# cmd.exe seeks through a batch file as it runs. With LF-only endings that
# seek can land mid-line, which breaks `goto` into labels and the multi-line
# `if (...) else (...)` and `for /l ... do (...)` blocks this launcher is
# built from.
#
# `-text`, not `text eol=crlf`: `text eol=crlf` stores the blob normalised to
# LF and converts on checkout, which leaves the CRLF depending on whoever
# generates the download. `-text` disables conversion, so the real CRLF bytes
# are what a clone, a raw download and GitHub's Download ZIP all hand over.
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text

# Shell scripts must stay LF, even when cloned on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.command text eol=lf
